1
00:03:07,741 --> 00:03:13,741
An unforgettable journey she probably won't remember.

2
00:06:15,483 --> 00:06:21,483
Finding Dory is a adventure, animation, comedy film directed by Andrew Stanton.

3
00:09:23,225 --> 00:09:29,225
Dory is reunited with her friends Nemo and Marlin in
the search for answers about her past.

4
00:12:30,967 --> 00:12:36,967
What can she remember?

5
00:15:38,709 --> 00:15:44,709
Who are her parents?

6
00:18:46,451 --> 00:18:52,451
And where did she learn to speak Whale?

7
00:21:54,193 --> 00:22:00,193
Marlin (voice), played by Albert Brooks.

8
00:25:01,935 --> 00:25:07,935
Dory (voice), played by Ellen DeGeneres.

9
00:28:09,677 --> 00:28:15,677
Hank (voice), played by Ed O'Neill.

10
00:31:17,419 --> 00:31:23,419
Nemo (voice), played by Hayden Rolence.

11
00:34:25,161 --> 00:34:31,161
Jenny (voice), played by Diane Keaton.

12
00:37:32,903 --> 00:37:38,903
Charlie (voice), played by Eugene Levy.

13
00:40:40,645 --> 00:40:46,645
Finding Dory is a 2016 American animated comedy-drama adventure film
produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.

14
00:43:48,387 --> 00:43:54,387
It was directed by Andrew Stanton, co-directed by Angus MacLane, produced by
Lindsey Collins, and written by Stanton and Victoria Strouse.

15
00:46:56,129 --> 00:47:02,129
The film is both a sequel and spin-off following
the events of Finding Nemo (2003).

16
00:50:03,870 --> 00:50:09,870
Ellen DeGeneres (in her final film role prior to her retirement in 2024) and Albert Brooks reprise their roles from the first film, with Ed
O'Neill, Kaitlin Olson, Hayden Rolence (replacing Alexander Gould), Ty Burrell, Diane Keaton and Eugene Levy joining the cast.

17
00:53:11,612 --> 00:53:17,612
The film focuses on the amnesiac fish Dory (DeGeneres), who journeys
to be reunited with her parents (Keaton and Levy).

18
00:56:19,354 --> 00:56:25,354
Disney planned to make a sequel to Finding Nemo since 2005, tasking its new
studio Circle Seven Animation after disagreements with Pixar.

19
00:59:27,096 --> 00:59:33,096
Though it never went into production, a script was uploaded to the official Raindance
Film Festival website that includes elements of the unmade script.

20
01:02:34,838 --> 01:02:40,838
Disney's acquisition of Pixar in early 2006 led to the
cancellation of Circle Seven's version of the film.

21
01:05:42,580 --> 01:05:48,580
A Pixar-made sequel was announced in April 2013 as the
schedule for a November 2015 release.

22
01:08:50,322 --> 01:08:56,322
The fictional Marine Life Institute depicted extensively in the film is based on the production team's
research trips to the Monterey Bay Aquarium, the Marine Mammal Center and the Vancouver Aquarium.

23
01:11:58,064 --> 01:12:04,064
Thomas Newman returned to compose the score.

24
01:15:05,806 --> 01:15:11,806
Finding Dory premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on June 8, 2016,
and was released in theaters in the United States on June 17.

25
01:18:13,548 --> 01:18:19,548
It received widespread praise from critics, like its predecessor, for
its animation, emotional weight, voice acting and humor.

26
01:21:21,290 --> 01:21:27,290
The film earned $1.029 billion worldwide, finishing its theatrical run as the
third-highest-grossing film of 2016 and the fourth-highest-grossing animated film at the time.

27
01:24:29,032 --> 01:24:35,032
It set numerous box office records, including the biggest opening for an animated film in Canada and the
United States and the highest-grossing animated film in Canada and the United States.

28
01:27:36,774 --> 01:27:42,774
The film received a win at the 2017 Kids' Choice Awards for Favorite
Animated Movie, among various other awards at various shows.

29
01:30:44,516 --> 01:30:50,516
The film explores themes of fish, amnesia, octopus, sequel, anthropomorphism.

30
01:33:52,258 --> 01:33:58,258
The tone is lighthearted.
